<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 08:55:02 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>Bordeaux evacuates 55,000 more as fires worsen in France and Spain</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260725-french-pm-orders-deployment-of-a400m-military-transport-plane-to-help-battle-fires</link><description>
More than 300,000 people fled wildfires raging across France and Spain on Saturday as worsening conditions forced fresh evacuations. Fire-generated whirlwinds fuelled blazes near Bordeaux, while Spain battled expanding infernos threatening areas near Madrid. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25fe2234-88b4-11f1-a8fa-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C37M2T3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25fe2234-88b4-11f1-a8fa-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C37M2T3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b8f5b28-8803-11f1-b97f-915c535ddd7f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 08:54:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25fe2234-88b4-11f1-a8fa-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C37M2T3.jpg">AFP - FLORIAN PLAUCHEUR</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ecowas greenlights $25bn Nigeria-Morocco mega gas pipeline</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260726-ecowas-greenlights-25bn-mega-gas-pipeline-nigeria-morocco</link><description>
West African leaders have approved plans for a gas pipeline linking Nigeria to Morocco, marking a major political milestone for one of Africa's most ambitious infrastructure projects.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5fc30d46-85d9-11f1-b888-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8293056.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5fc30d46-85d9-11f1-b888-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8293056.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">596d58c6-851f-11f1-8b17-3366361549e6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 08:54:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5fc30d46-85d9-11f1-b888-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8293056.jpg">AFP - FLORIAN PLAUCHEUR</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>One dead and several injured at Berlin's LGBTQ+ march after a car drives into the crowd</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260725-several-people-are-injured-at-berlin-s-lgbtq-march-after-a-car-drives-into-the-crowd</link><description>
A van slammed into people gathered for Berlin’s famed Pride festival on Saturday night, killing one person, injuring at least 16 others and prompting police to call off the celebrations and a concert in the German capital hours after they had begun.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6f180202-8871-11f1-a840-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26206759570452.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6f180202-8871-11f1-a840-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26206759570452.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24d70508-8871-11f1-b3a1-f192ae8cdfbf</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 21:42:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6f180202-8871-11f1-a840-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26206759570452.jpg">Fabian Sommer/DPA via AP - Fabian Sommer</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Senegal ready to show ‘what it is capable of’ at Dakar 2026 Youth Olympics</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260726-senegal-ready-to-show-what-it-is-capable-of-at-dakar-2026-youth-olympics</link><description>
With venues nearing completion and public enthusiasm growing, Dakar 2026 chief organiser Ibrahima Wade tells RFI that Senegal is ready to make Olympic history when the Youth Games begin on 31 October.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e138c88-8655-11f1-9023-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-93F67HH-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e138c88-8655-11f1-9023-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-93F67HH-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c11d46d6-866c-11f1-8b0d-07709273a6e7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 05:14:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e138c88-8655-11f1-9023-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-93F67HH-1.jpg">AFP - SEYLLOU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Climate change 'exacerbating' drought across Europe, scientists say</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260725-climate-change-exacerbating-drought-across-europe-scientists-say</link><description>
Climate change is exacerbating drought in Europe as extreme heat evaporates water supplies, scientists said in a study published this week, with low water levels disrupting shipping, farming and industry in countries including Romania and Greece.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33dfd932-8437-11f1-a066-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T071512Z-1618978233-RC28HMARUIOU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-ROMANIA-DROUGHT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33dfd932-8437-11f1-a066-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T071512Z-1618978233-RC28HMARUIOU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-ROMANIA-DROUGHT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b5aee396-8675-11f1-8500-07980066211b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 08:58:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33dfd932-8437-11f1-a066-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T071512Z-1618978233-RC28HMARUIOU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-ROMANIA-DROUGHT.jpg">© Inquam Photos / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Iran seeks to 'sow confusion among Gulf states' by targeting Bahrain and Kuwait</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260725-iran-seeks-to-sow-confusion-among-gulf-states-by-targeting-bahrain-and-kuwait</link><description>
As Iranian drones and missiles target Bahrain and Kuwait, RFI spoke with Mahdi Ghuloom of the Dubai-based ORF Middle East think tank, who believes long-standing tensions, the small size of the two countries and divisions over how the Gulf should respond are playing their part in this development. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0024bd0e-8434-11f1-be61-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2J77CU-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0024bd0e-8434-11f1-be61-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2J77CU-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7dd28f3e-8681-11f1-8344-157a6b6090b8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 14:22:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0024bd0e-8434-11f1-be61-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2J77CU-1.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>More health workers strike as Ebola cases in Congo near 3,000, including over 1,300 deaths</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260725-more-health-workers-strike-as-ebola-cases-in-congo-near-3-000-including-over-1-300-deaths</link><description>
Health workers at an Ebola treatment center in eastern Congo went on strike Saturday over payment issues, disrupting care for patients in the epicenter of the country’s rapidly growing outbreak.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7a0aa694-8833-11f1-a8ad-1172a0685593</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 14:21:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg">AP Photo/Dirole Lotsima Dieudonn - Dirole Lotsima Dieudonne</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Israel's move to recognise Armenian genocide stalls under regional pressure</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260725-israel-s-move-to-recognise-armenian-genocide-stalls-under-regional-pressure</link><description>
The Israeli parliament's decision to postpone a vote on recognising the Armenian genocide by Ottoman Turkey is being seen as a triumph for regional diplomacy, as Azerbaijan in particular seeks to avert a further escalation in tensions between its close allies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dfc0b862-8756-11f1-8b1e-b11ae43ab3b1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 11:44:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Haitians at home and abroad fear fallout from end of US protection</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260725-haitians-in-port-au-prince-and-new-york-fear-fallout-from-end-of-us-protectionn</link><description>
Concern is mounting in Haiti and in the United States ahead of the planned end of Temporary Protected Status for Haitians on 27 July, which could leave nearly 350,000 people at risk of deportation from the US.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/263c440c-871e-11f1-bf13-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26190726418960.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/263c440c-871e-11f1-bf13-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26190726418960.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e873a4d2-8748-11f1-89df-852f3d9356bc</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 06:18:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/263c440c-871e-11f1-bf13-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26190726418960.jpg">© Gregory Bull / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>NGOs take France to court over companies’ links to Israeli settlements</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260725-ngos-take-france-to-court-over-companies-links-to-israeli-settlements</link><description>
Five NGOs on Wednesday filed a case before France’s highest administrative court, seeking a ruling that would oblige the French government to take measures preventing French companies and economic institutions from conducting commercial activities in Israeli settlements.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/454f7950-4dc5-11f1-aa92-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-07T141701Z-762897800-RC264LA4QWMF-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-WEST-BANK-SETTLEMENTS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/454f7950-4dc5-11f1-aa92-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-07T141701Z-762897800-RC264LA4QWMF-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-WEST-BANK-SETTLEMENTS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0118c00a-867a-11f1-99a1-a577b3d6e10b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 05:17:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/454f7950-4dc5-11f1-aa92-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-07T141701Z-762897800-RC264LA4QWMF-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-WEST-BANK-SETTLEMENTS.jpg">© Mussa Qawasma/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Heatwave hits North Africa, with power cuts in Tunisia and wildfires in Algeria</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260724-heatwave-hits-north-africa-with-power-cuts-in-tunisia-and-wildfires-in-algeria</link><description>
In Tunisia long power outages across the country have added to the strain of an intense heatwave, with temperatures as high as 49C. In neighbouring Algeria, more than 100 people were hospitalised after wildfires, the country's interior minister said this week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98e62ef2-873a-11f1-9b15-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria-fire-july2026-afp-000-C2QK7EK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98e62ef2-873a-11f1-9b15-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria-fire-july2026-afp-000-C2QK7EK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84103238-8736-11f1-a751-f3778ee5cdf9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 21:04:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98e62ef2-873a-11f1-9b15-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria-fire-july2026-afp-000-C2QK7EK.jpg">AFP - -</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Notre-Dame's disputed new windows 'on schedule' for December reveal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260724-notre-dame-s-disputed-new-windows-on-schedule-for-december-reveal</link><description>
Six contemporary stained-glass windows designed by artist Claire Tabouret for Notre-Dame de Paris cathedral will be installed between October and November, then unveiled to the public in December, the public body overseeing the cathedral's restoration announced on Thursday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6658e264-dc30-11f0-a7ba-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Photo-d-en-t%C3%AAte-3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6658e264-dc30-11f0-a7ba-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Photo-d-en-t%C3%AAte-3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f49570c-873e-11f1-80df-81678484cde9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 10:04:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6658e264-dc30-11f0-a7ba-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Photo-d-en-t%C3%AAte-3.jpg">© Baptiste Coulon/RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Record June heatwave sees France record 'unprecedented' 5,764 excess deaths</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260724-record-june-heatwave-sees-france-record-unprecedented-5-764-excess-deaths</link><description>
France recorded 5,764 more deaths than usual during a record-breaking heatwave last month, health authorities have said, describing the excess mortality among people aged 15 and older as “unprecedented”.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/65570742-8356-11f1-b3b2-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-26T100255Z-1708830565-RC241MA96SCW-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-HOT-HOMES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/65570742-8356-11f1-b3b2-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-26T100255Z-1708830565-RC241MA96SCW-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-HOT-HOMES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">923265a6-867e-11f1-b56a-1d8a95e117a7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:55:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/65570742-8356-11f1-b3b2-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-26T100255Z-1708830565-RC241MA96SCW-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-HOT-HOMES.jpg">REUTERS - Gonzalo Fuentes</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Macky Sall pledges to restore trust in UN as leadership race gathers pace</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260724-macky-sall-pledges-to-restore-trust-in-un-as-leadership-race-gathers-pace</link><description>
Former Senegalese president Macky Sall has pledged to restore trust in the United Nations and make the organisation more responsive, as he seeks to become the first African to lead the global body in almost three decades.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e79d091c-8730-11f1-95c6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3244NM-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e79d091c-8730-11f1-95c6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3244NM-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5fb0d170-8729-11f1-a14a-8729fd06c85d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 07:05:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e79d091c-8730-11f1-95c6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3244NM-1.jpg">AFP - LEONARDO MUNOZ</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>European Union slams 'inflammatory' Houthi Red Sea tanker attack</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260724-european-union-slams-inflammatory-houthi-red-sea-tanker-attack</link><description>
The European Union's top diplomat demanded on Thursday that the Houthis cease attacks on ships in the Red Sea, after a Saudi vessel was hit by the Iran-backed rebels.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/13b15678-6343-11f1-85d9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A4Y769F.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/13b15678-6343-11f1-85d9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A4Y769F.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">459b07b0-8698-11f1-afee-8b7d96a4f501</guid><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 06:08:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/13b15678-6343-11f1-85d9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A4Y769F.jpg">AFP - MOHAMMED HUWAIS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ghanaians ask ICC to investigate xenophobic violence in South Africa</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260724-ghanaians-ask-icc-to-investigate-xenophobic-violence-in-south-africa</link><description>
Two Ghanaian nationals have petitioned the International Criminal Court to open a preliminary investigation into attacks on foreign nationals in South Africa, arguing the violence could amount to crimes against humanity, as Ghana's president repeated his call on Thursday for the African Union to address the ongoing unrest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2c307f66-7c12-11f1-9589-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-09T111435Z-177337990-RC29AMAPR5F1-RTRMADP-3-SAFRICA-XENOPHOBIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2c307f66-7c12-11f1-9589-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-09T111435Z-177337990-RC29AMAPR5F1-RTRMADP-3-SAFRICA-XENOPHOBIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9a45fb74-866d-11f1-b5d0-5ba20fd9084b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 08:58:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2c307f66-7c12-11f1-9589-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-09T111435Z-177337990-RC29AMAPR5F1-RTRMADP-3-SAFRICA-XENOPHOBIA.jpg">© REUTERS - Oupa Nkosi </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Wildfire sees 12,000 residents and tourists evacuated in south-west France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260723-wildfire-in-france-at-least-12-000-evacuated-in-the-south-west</link><description>
A wildfire near Bordeaux in south-west France has led to the evacuation of a further 7,000 people on Thursday, bringing the total number of tourists and residents moved to 12,000, local authorities said.
